    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d77-a5">

                <pb facs="0239" n="111" xml:id="pg111"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Commodore Wiltse to
                        Surgeon Penrose and Lieutenant
                    Wood</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. S. Swatara</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps">third
                                rate</hi>),<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Livingston,
                            Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1885-03-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 13,
                    1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: You are hereby appointed a board to
                    ascertain the condition of the destitute American citizens and foreigners in the
                    vicinity of Livingston and Puerto Barrios, Guatemala.</p>
                <p>You will find out those who are in immediate need of food, clothing, and
                    medicine, also those who desire to return to New Orleans, and report the result
                    of your investigations to me.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>G. C. WILTSE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Commander, United States
                            Navy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
